ities), precedence/associativity identities, lexical corner cases.\n- **§11 Normative test oracle** — 18 valid and 12 invalid inputs with expected outcomes.\n- **§12** — non-normative notes (recursion limits, ℤ via Python `int`).\n\n**Verification**: Ran a conformance script covering every §11 oracle row, the §9-C4 indicative messages, P8 precedence/associativity identities (200 randomized cases), P7 algebraic laws (100 randomized cases), and P9 lexical corners — all pass. One initial test-script failure was a bug in the test's own algebra, not in the implementation or spec; fixed and re-verified.\n\n**Notes**: The spec is implementation-first, so it and `expr_eval.py` are currently consistent; if the implementation changes, re-run the oracle checks in §11."